cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it together with the two sources of the proof it reads (see references)."
title: "RHStructure: primes in short intervals from the Lean proof of the Riemann Hypothesis"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 deduction, from Mathlib's RiemannHypothesis, of psi(x) = x + O(x^(1/2+delta)) and of a
  prime in (x, x + x^(1/2+epsilon)] for large x (von Koch 1901), holding without hypotheses with
  RH supplied by grh-compact. Also a structural reading, in the language of rings and arcs, of the Lean 4 proof of the Riemann
  Hypothesis and of GRH for Dirichlet L-functions by Levent Alpoge (with Claude), in the
  compact rewriting grh-compact by Luke Sernau and colleagues at Anthropic (with Claude).
  The Lean files under Structural/ build on the unchanged grh-compact and state the chain of
  the proof in ring and arc terms, including the lever that fixes the exponent 1/2. The proof
  of the Riemann Hypothesis is not a result of this work.
type: software
authors:
